<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Supreme Council of the Republic of Lithuania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1990">1990</a>–<a href="/years/1992">1992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Reconstituent Seimas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Supreme <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-lithuania">Council of Lithuania</a> was the parliament elected in February 1990 with a majority for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajudis">Sąjūdis</a> movement, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vytautas-landsbergis">Vytautas Landsbergis</a> as chairman. On 11 March 1990 it declared the restoration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>'s independence, the first Soviet republic to do so. It withstood a Soviet economic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> and the January 1991 attack in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> before international recognition in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/supreme-council-of-the-republic-of-lithuania.jpg" alt="Supreme Council of the Republic of Lithuania" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Lithuania_(1990%E2%80%931991).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
